  <content>
    <procedure>
      <commonInfo>
        <title>Job description</title>
        <para>This section gives the procedure to repair the Small Areas of damaged paint.</para>
        <para>The repair scheme shown below is intended for repairs to small areas of damaged paint of less than 5806.44 mm² (9 in²) area and isolated from other areas of damaged by minimum 304.80 mm (12 in). It is possible that the finished repair will not be to the initial production quality standard.</para>
        <note>
          <notePara>For larger repairs refer to Safran Seats France.</notePara>
        </note>
        <para />
        <note>
          <notePara>This repair is for small areas of damaged paint contained in a maximum area of 76.2 x 76.2 mm (3 x 3 in). The damaged paint must be a minimum of 304.80 mm (12 in) away from other areas of damage.</notePara>
        </note>
        <para />
      </commonInfo>
      <preliminaryRqmts>
        <reqCondGroup>
          <noConds />
        </reqCondGroup>
        <reqSupportEquips>
          <noSupportEquips />
        </reqSupportEquips>
        <reqSupplies>
          <noSupplies />
        </reqSupplies>
        <reqSpares>
          <noSpares />
        </reqSpares>
        <reqSafety>
          <safetyRqmts>
            <note>
              <notePara>Only approved personnel must do the maintenance to the component.</notePara>
            </note>
          </safetyRqmts>
        </reqSafety>
      </preliminaryRqmts>
      <mainProcedure>
        <proceduralStep>
          <title>Procedure</title>
          <proceduralStep>
            <title>Small areas of damaged paint repair procedure</title>
            <warning>
              <warningAndCautionPara>Do all paint/lacquer spray-gun procedures in an area
with good airflow. do not breathe paint/solvent fumes and use manufacturer’s
recommended breathing masks and equipment. obey health and safety
warning recommended by the manufacturer and the local health and
safety regulator. obey applicable fire precautions. this will help
prevent injury.</warningAndCautionPara>
            </warning>
            <warning>
              <warningAndCautionPara>when you use cleaning agents, obey the manufacturer’s
instructions.</warningAndCautionPara>
            </warning>
            <caution>
              <warningAndCautionPara>when you use fillers, primers and paints, obey the
manufacturer’s instructions.</warningAndCautionPara>
            </caution>
            <caution>
              <warningAndCautionPara>do not clean the repaired area for 48 hours.</warningAndCautionPara>
            </caution>
            <proceduralStep>
              <para>Remove paint back to the surface of the material.</para>
            </proceduralStep>
            <proceduralStep>
              <para>Prepare surface to the paint manufacturer’s instructions.</para>
            </proceduralStep>
            <proceduralStep>
              <para>Apply a layer of filler, refer to <dmRef><dmRefIdent><dmCode modelIdentCode="B7772S11MON" systemDiffCode="A" systemCode="25" subSystemCode="3" subSubSystemCode="0" assyCode="12" disassyCode="01" disassyCodeVariant="005" infoCode="040" infoCodeVariant="A" itemLocationCode="C" /></dmRefIdent><dmRefAddressItems><dmTitle><techName>Front Row Monument Assembly</techName><infoName>Trim and Finish</infoName></dmTitle></dmRefAddressItems></dmRef>, to the paint manufacturer’s instructions.</para>
            </proceduralStep>
            <proceduralStep>
              <para>Prepare surface to the paint manufacturer’s instructions.</para>
            </proceduralStep>
            <proceduralStep>
              <para>Apply a layer of primer, refer to <dmRef><dmRefIdent><dmCode modelIdentCode="B7772S11MON" systemDiffCode="A" systemCode="25" subSystemCode="3" subSubSystemCode="0" assyCode="12" disassyCode="01" disassyCodeVariant="005" infoCode="040" infoCodeVariant="A" itemLocationCode="C" /></dmRefIdent><dmRefAddressItems><dmTitle><techName>Front Row Monument Assembly</techName><infoName>Trim and Finish</infoName></dmTitle></dmRefAddressItems></dmRef>, to the paint manufacturer’s instructions.</para>
            </proceduralStep>
            <proceduralStep>
              <para>Prepare surface to the paint manufacturer’s instructions.</para>
            </proceduralStep>
            <proceduralStep>
              <para>Apply a layer of top coat paint, refer to <dmRef><dmRefIdent><dmCode modelIdentCode="B7772S11MON" systemDiffCode="A" systemCode="25" subSystemCode="3" subSubSystemCode="0" assyCode="12" disassyCode="01" disassyCodeVariant="005" infoCode="040" infoCodeVariant="A" itemLocationCode="C" /></dmRefIdent><dmRefAddressItems><dmTitle><techName>Front Row Monument Assembly</techName><infoName>Trim and Finish</infoName></dmTitle></dmRefAddressItems></dmRef>, to the paint manufacturer’s instructions.</para>
            </proceduralStep>
            <proceduralStep>
              <para>Finish surface to the paint manufacturer’s instructions.</para>
            </proceduralStep>
          </proceduralStep>
        </proceduralStep>
      </mainProcedure>
      <closeRqmts>
        <reqCondGroup>
          <noConds />
        </reqCondGroup>
      </closeRqmts>
    </procedure>
